hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2700","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yahya, who narrated to us Ibn al-Aṣbahānī, who narrated to us ʿAbd al-Raḥīm [Ibn Sulaymān], on the authority of ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUthmān ibn Khuthaym, who informed us Abū Ṭufayl (RA). [The narrator relates:] I asked Abū Ṭufayl (RA) about the practice of raml (brisk walking) performed during the three circuits of the Kaʿbah, and he reported that Ibn ʿAbbās (RA) informed him: ""When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) arrived [in Mecca] during the treaty of Quraysh, and upon entering Mecca he entered through this great gate, while the people of Quraysh were seated in the area adjacent to the Ḥajar [the Black Stone] or al-Ḥijr [the enclosed space adjoining the Kaʿbah]."" [Abū Ṭufayl (RA)] then recounted the full narration of the hadith. Abū Bakr [the compiler of the collection] stated: ""I did not specify in my compilation whether the reference was to the Ḥajar or al-Ḥijr."""
